# ================= 0.3.23 TreeFortMig: the ONE-TIME Fortune refund of a profile (readFile; research/Metals-Tools-Fortune-Spec.md 2.1) =========
# Mining.MFortune / Smithing.SSmelt went to max 10. A profile ABOVE a node's max keeps its levels saved (TreeCalc.eff uses the max, as
# before) and gets the Dust paid for the levels above the max back as that tree's Dust credit (levels cost B x n^3 Dust from n to n + 1; the
# token only paid the unlock). Only once the trees.properties update ran / found its marker this start (CFGOK), History copy first
# (history/fortune323/<key>.properties, verified), then the credit + fort323 (fort.r323=done) + d.mig (saved within 10 s); one INFO line +
# one fortune323-changes.log line with the Undo steps. Never throws.
# IDEMPOTENT (critic L1): the Dust refunded so far per tree sits in Class.SkyyFortune.paid323 (a Class.* line of an unknown class: 0.3.x
# builds keep it and write it back, while 0.3.22 drops fort.r323) - a refund pays only what is owed minus what that line already paid.
F(fmig, "public static volatile boolean CFGOK = false;")   # set by TreeMig323.run (this start's max values are the 0.3.23 ones or an admin's)
F(fmig, "public static volatile long APPLIED = 0L;")
F(fmig, "public static volatile long SNAPFAILS = 0L;")
F(fmig, "public static volatile String LAST = \"\";")
F(fmig, "public static final String PAID = \"Class.SkyyFortune.paid323\";")
